{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-101702-r4514096","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Madbucha (North African Peppers and Tomatoes)","sourcePageId":101702,"sourceRevision":"4514096","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:42:59Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Madbucha%20(North%20African%20Peppers%20and%20Tomatoes)&oldid=4514096","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:19.708Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Appetizer recipes","Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:North African recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bell pepper","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using onion","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Side dish recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"c7a3afa92b1aa5006efcd5044f526f595121608dd0289e79f947b70e29afeed9","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Vegetable recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Madbucha''' or '''matbucha''' is a North African dish of stewed tomatoes and peppers. It can be used as a side dish with meats, as well as put on bread or white rice. There's more than one way to make it, and the following recipe is a family recipe. \n\n==Ingredients==\n*[[Cookbook:Oil and fat|Oil]]\n*2 [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]s, [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*2 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], chopped\n*15 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], [[Cookbook:Cube|cubed]]\n*10 [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]], cut into small pieces\n*5 [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile peppers]], chopped small\n*330 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] canned [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]]\n*[[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n*[[Cookbook:Pepper|Pepper]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cumin|Cumin]]\n*[[Cookbook:Parsley|Parsley]]\n*[[Cookbook:Oregano|Oregano]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Take a pot that is big enough for all of the above ingredients, cover the bottom with oil, and put it on a flame.\n#When the oil gets hot, add the onion and garlic. \n#When they start to fry, add the rest of the vegetables and salt.\n#Mix it up a bit and cover the pot.\n#Leave it to cook, mixing it every so often, until the level of the liquid is higher than the level of the vegetables.\n#Drain off most (but not all) the liquid.\n#Add the tomato paste and the spices.\n#Mix, and let it cool.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* When chopping the peppers, you want them small but not so small that they disappear when cooked.\n* The peppers can be any color, but red is traditional.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Appetizer recipes]]\n[[Category:North African recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Madbucha (North African Peppers and Tomatoes)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Oil","sourceText":"Oil","amountText":"Oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","n